["https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/FunctionalSafety/VerificationType/inspection", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment", "A thorough examination or checking of documentation, records, processes, or systems to confirm compliance or adherence. An inspection needs to have a defined set of acceptance criteria (e.g. a checklist), a documentation of roles involved in the inspection (e.g. to document the inspector's independence) and a clear documentation of when and how it was performed.", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/Core/RelationshipType/hasConcludedLicense", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label", "hasConcludedLicense", "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string", "", ""]
["_:N1812abfade2d40f78d3ba4010f2e9693", "http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#class", "https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/Core/Bom", "globalId", "", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/Core/ExternalIdentifierType/ismn", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment", "[International Standard Music Number (ISMN)](https://ismn-international.org/ismn/the-ismn/) is a unique numeric identifier for printed music (notated music) standardized by [ISO 10957](https://www.iso.org/standard/83122.html). It consists of either 10 characters (starting with the letter \"M\" for assignments prior to January 1, 2008) or 13 digits. A 13-digit ISMN is composed of four parts: the GS1 prefix `979-0`, a registrant element, an item element, and a check digit. While elements may be divided by spaces or hyphens for human readability, these separators shall be omitted when the identifier is stored electronically (e.g., `9790006538424`).", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/Core/CreationInfo", "http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#property", "_:N4e7dd07b375c4eb2acf11a0ce1ef2b31", "localId", "", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/Software/SbomType/deployed", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment", "SBOM provides an inventory of software that is present on a system. This may be an assembly of other SBOMs that combines analysis of configuration options, and examination of execution behavior in a (potentially simulated) deployment environment.", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
